# reasons.vstd: what only the developer can state.  A contract between two methods of one class, an
# annotation Python never checks, a named assumption.  Polish checks each one against the code; a
# reason that cites an annotation or an assumption is DOCUMENTED at most and is bound (`bound`) to the
# code it was written against, so any edit there makes it STALE until someone looks again.

reason session-evaluate-contract
  claim    contract src/verifier/core/evidence.py::VerificationSession.evaluate `mechanism.evaluate` supplier src/verifier/core/evidence.py::VerificationSession.register mechanism
  basis    registry
  falsify  plant fs-write in src/verifier/domains/contracts/actor_closure.py::_ActorClosureMechanism.evaluate expect named
  falsify  mutate delete-basis expect reopen
  note     evaluate runs only a mechanism some caller registered; each caller that builds its own
  note     session and registers project classes reaches exactly what it registered

reason session-compound-contract
  claim    contract src/verifier/core/evidence.py::VerificationSession.evaluate_compound `evaluator` supplier src/verifier/core/evidence.py::VerificationSession.register mechanism
  basis    registry
  falsify  mutate delete-basis expect reopen
  note     evaluator is getattr(mechanism, "evaluate_compound", None) behind a callable() guard; a
  note     registered class without the method runs nothing there unless __getattr__ or an outside base supplies one

