reason text-value-assumed
  claim    type src/verifier/domains/common.py::text:62:42 `value` str
  basis    guard
  assume   isinstance-means-exact
  falsify  mutate delete-basis expect reopen
  bound    sha256:6ceb4de6f08c0721f16f8528762cdb0e4a49f3e347a4590a55ce808e40b7a797
  note     isinstance admits subclasses of str: no subject subclass overrides strip, and values from outside
  note     the subject are assumed exact.  The project's own tests break that assumption on purpose
  note     (tests/test_retained_selection.py ArmedString overrides strip): a witness, listed, not refuting.
  note     `type(value) is not str` would make this ESTABLISHED with no assumption
